seccomp-base.json — vendored upstream seccomp profile
=====================================================

This is the default seccomp profile from the containers/common project
(used by Podman, Buildah and CRI-O), vendored verbatim as the base from
which the OpenWrt container floor is rendered.

Source:  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/containers/common/main/pkg/seccomp/seccomp.json
Repo:    https://github.com/containers/common
Path:    pkg/seccomp/seccomp.json
Commit:  a5ccdae846b629b5ceaefa6ffd5c6511409c3487  (2025-08-27)
Fetched: 2026-06-04

The file is kept byte-for-byte as upstream so it can be diffed against a
later upstream revision. Do NOT hand-edit it; re-fetch to update, then
re-review seccomp-tighten.list against any new syscalls.

The OpenWrt floor is NOT this file. seccomp-render.uc resolves this
profile for a single target architecture, with an EMPTY capability set
(the floor drops all capabilities), and then removes the syscalls listed
in seccomp-tighten.list before emitting the ujail-consumable OCI seccomp
object. The tightening is the security delta; this file is only the
starting point.

